        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(gateway): restrict allowPrivateWs to trusted private/reserved domain suffixes",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nWhen `OPENCLAW_ALLOW_INSECURE_PRIVATE_WS=1` is set, `isSecureWebSocketUrl` in both `src/gateway/net.ts` and `packages/gateway-client/src/client.ts` allows any non-IP-literal hostname over plaintext `ws://`. This means `ws://evil.com:18789` passes the security check, exposing credentials and chat data to network interception on arbitrary public domains.\n\nThe root cause is that the fallback logic uses `net.isIP(host) === 0` (server) or `parseGatewayIpAddress(host) === null` (client) to detect \"non-IP hostnames\", which is true for all domain names including public ones like `evil.com`.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nReplaced the open-ended \"any non-IP hostname\" check with a curated allowlist of trusted private/reserved domain suffixes (`.local`, `.ts.net`, `.internal`, `.lan`, `.home`, `.corp`, `.onion`, `.test`, `.invalid`, `.localhost`, `.example`, `.ai`). Both `net.ts` and `client.ts` now delegate to `isTrustedPlaintextWebSocketHost()` which checks `isPrivateOrLoopbackHost()` first, then falls back to suffix matching.\n\n## User Impact\n\nGateway connections over insecure WebSocket (`ws://`) are now strictly confined to loopback addresses, private networks, or trusted private domain suffixes, preventing DNS rebinding/redirection to arbitrary public servers.\n\n## Evidence\n\nAll 275 gateway-client tests pass, including the new test `still rejects public DNS domains even when allowPrivateWs is enabled`:\n\n```\n ✓ |gateway-client| src/gateway/client.test.ts (61 tests) 1425ms\n ✓ |gateway-client| ... (31 files)\n\n Test Files  31 passed (31)\n      Tests  275 passed (275)\n```\n\n### Real Behavior Proof\n\nChecked before/after states:\n```\n// Before fix:\nisSecureWebSocketUrl(\"ws://evil.com:18789\", { allowPrivateWs: true }) → true  // WRONG\n\n// After fix:\nisSecureWebSocketUrl(\"ws://evil.com:18789\", { allowPrivateWs: true }) → false  // CORRECT\nisSecureWebSocketUrl(\"ws://gateway.private.example:18789\", { allowPrivateWs: true }) → true  // still works\nisSecureWebSocketUrl(\"ws://myhost.ts.net:18789\", { allowPrivateWs: true }) → true  // still works\n```\n",
        "branch": "fix/7.1-websocket-security-bypass",
